# Mola Mola Diving Center – Manual Testing Project

## Project Overview

This project documents the manual QA testing performed on the Mola Mola Diving Center website, covering its main functionality, user journeys, booking process, navigation, and content presentation.

**Website:** https://molamoladivingcenter.com/

**Developed by:** [Deviora Studio](https://deviorastudio.com/)

**Manual Testing by:** Ali Mohamed Abdelsalam

**Date:** October 2026

## Testing Scope

The manual testing process covered:

- Website navigation and linked pages
- Trip, course, and package information
- Booking functionality and input validation
- Contact forms and information
- Gallery and content visibility
- Responsive presentation
- End-to-end user journeys

## Test Execution Summary

| Metric | Result |
|---|---:|
| Total Test Cases | 166 |
| Executed | 166 |
| Passed | 154 |
| Failed | 12 |
| Execution Rate | 100% |
| Pass Rate | 92.77% |
| Bug Report Entries | 12 |

## Bug Reporting

The bug-tracking workbook documents 12 failed test cases, including issues related to:

- Content visibility on linked pages
- Contact and map information
- Booking field validation
- Course and package booking selection

Two reported items require further requirement confirmation: private-trip pricing behavior and the intended Dive Trips URL. Some reported issues may share the same root cause.

## Project Deliverables

| Deliverable | Description |
|---|---|
| Test Cases | Documented manual test cases and execution results |
| Bug Report | Reported issues with reproduction steps, expected and actual results |
| Final QA Report | Testing overview, execution metrics, findings, and conclusion |

## Tools Used

- Microsoft Excel
- Manual Testing
- Bug Tracking

## Conclusion

Manual testing was completed with 166 executed test cases, achieving a 92.77% pass rate. The documented results provide an overview of the website's tested functionality and identify areas requiring fixes or further clarification.

